TIP:  Trill the (D/A) in the intro and when you see it in combination with a (D/A)(A) in the verse.  (D/A) is just regular (D) with your pinky added to the 4th string/4th fret.  Regular (D) can be played in place of (D/A) and also in place of the (Bm) if you wish.

TIP:  The (Amaj7) is one you don’t play often.  Hitting the index finger on the 1st fret/3rd string is the key.  The middle and ring fingers will then come naturally.  I find it helps to think "(D7)" moved up one string-set.


